      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WIZARD'S STAR (8) has the best recent profile despite still chasing a first win. His third at the Kenso two starts back had merit after he began slowly and was held up over 1800m. Worked hard from the wide draw and knocked up with a dismal sixth in a C1 at Newcastle. Top three contender. FRANKIE'S BOY (6) is the clear danger after leading and being beaten only a 1.5 lens at Goulburn on soft ground with the 58kg. His third-up fitness and the Waterhouse-Bott polish will make him hard to catch. POWERFUL PRAYER (2) deep into the campaign and brings the strongest established staying record, having gone close in BM64 grade and shown he is effective around this trip. Well drawn in a weaker race and stays in the calculations. WHAT SHE'S HAVING (10) is still a maiden, but her Hawkesbury fifth came after being held up and the jockey change plus weight relief give her a realistic opportunity to run into the placings.",
